# um-texts 1
=== PERK Actions
Actions
Actions determine both how swiftly a character can use his weapons and how quickly he can cast spells.

=== PERK Archery
Archery
The skill of using projectile weapons - bows and cross-bows. The outcome of a character's attack (the chances that he strikes enemies) is determined by his skill with this particular type of weapon (Skill) and affected by his Dexterity.

=== PERK Astral
Astral Magic
This skill allows you to create and use spells of the Astral Magic school. These are very different in nature - e.g. Healing or Paralysis. Magic abilities depend on skill in the particular magic school (Skill) and the character's Intelligence.

=== PERK Awareness
Awareness
Awareness

=== PERK Backstab
Backstab
A special skill which allows the character to make a lethal backstab at an enemy. If your character manages to get near the target from behind, he will automatically perform a backstab and cause much more damage than with common strikes.

=== PERK Dexterity
Dexterity
Dexterity determines a character's "Stamina" (the ability to use difficult spells) and "Actions" (how quickly the character can hit or cast spells). Dexterity also affects "Attack" and "Use/Steal" parameters.

=== PERK Elemental
Elemental Magic
A skill which allows you to create and use spells of the Elemental Magic school. Most destructive spells are in this category - e.g. Fireball. Magic abilities depend on the skill in a particular magic school (Skill) and the character's Intelligence.

=== PERK Encumbrance
Encumbrance:
The Encumbrance determines how much weight your character carries. The more armor and weapons he has and the heavier they are, the higher the character's encumbrance. If it exceeds the "Encumbrance" value (determined by the character's Strength), he cannot run.

=== PERK Experience
Experience
The higher the character's Experience is, the better his "Health" and "Stamina". Also, Experience can be used to increase Skills and Abilities. Experience gained during the game will be distributed equally among all members of your team, but its value will change according to the characters' Intelligence.

=== PERK Health
Health
Health determines how much damage your character can sustain. When damaged, the character's Health diminishes. When Health reaches 0 or less, the character dies.

=== PERK Intelligence
Intelligence
Intelligence determines the amount of experience your character can gain. The higher this value, the more experience is gained. Also, Intelligence affects the amount of Stamina used while casting spells (the higher the Intelligence, the less Stamina is spent). Intelligence also affects the "Knowledge of Magic" parameter.

=== PERK Mana
Stamina
Stamina determines a character's strength reserves. Characters with more stamina can cast more complex and difficult spells.

=== PERK Melee
Melee
The skill in using close combat weapons - knives, axes, spears etc. The outcome of a character's attack (the chances that he hits enemies) is determined by his skill with this particular type of weapon (Skill) and affected by his Dexterity.

=== PERK Move
Movement
Movement speed determines how quickly a character can move.

=== PERK Science
Use/Steal
A skill which allows the character to open locks, operate unfamiliar machinery and also steal things. It is based on Skill and affected by Dexterity. The higher this skill, the more complex devices your character can use, and the higher the chances that the enemy will not notice his loss.

=== PERK Sense
Sensory Magic
A skill which allows the character to create and use spells of the Sensory Magic school. These are mainly informational spells - e.g. Eagle Sight. Magic abilities depend on the skill in a particular magic school (Skill) and the character's Intelligence.

=== PERK Stealing
Stealing
Art of Thievery

=== PERK Stealth
Stealth
Stealth

=== PERK Strength
Strength
Strength affects characters' "Health" parameter - the higher their Strength, the more damage they can sustain. A High Strength value allows you to carry more weight, i.e. you can wear heavier armor.

=== PERK Tame
Taming
Taming

